"""Phase 4: assemble notes/phase4.md from saved results (price_of_recall.json, phase 2/3 json). python -I scripts/p4_02_write_notes.py"""
import json
import os
import sys

sys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())
import numpy as np

J = lambda p: json.load(open(p))
D, GS, C3, X3, FE = J("data/processed/phase4/price_of_recall.json"), J("data/processed/phase2/groups_summary.json"), J("data/processed/phase3/conformal.json"), J("data/processed/phase3/cascade.json"), J("data/processed/phase3/final_eval.json")
TASKS, R = ("thermal", "solvent", "water"), D["recalls"]
ci = lambda t: f"{t[0]:.3f} [{t[1]:.3f}, {t[2]:.3f}]"
L = []
w = L.append
w("# Phase 4: price of recall, limitations, and paper figures")
w("")
w("Generated by `scripts/p4_02_write_notes.py`. Numbers come from `scripts/p4_01_price_of_recall.py` (-> `data/processed/phase4/price_of_recall.json`) and from the saved Phase 2/3 results; figures are drawn by `figures/fig*.py` from saved files only (`bash figures/make_all.sh`), PDFs in `figures/`.")
w("")
w("## 1. Price of recall")
w("")
w("**Definition.** The price of a target recall r is the fraction of ALL MOFs that must be kept so that a fraction r of the truly stable MOFs is kept. Here it is computed with the threshold known exactly: t = the floor((1-r) n_pos)-th smallest positive score, kept = share of all MOFs with score >= t, on the pooled group-aware calibration + test MOFs. This isolates the discrimination of the scores from the noise of one calibration draw (the conformal single-split numbers are in `notes/phase2.md` and `notes/phase3.md`). Intervals are 95% percentile bootstrap intervals over **groups** (1,000 resamples).")
w("")
w("**Synthetic scores.** For each stage the real labels and real group ids of the pooled MOFs are kept; scores are drawn from a binormal model (negatives N(0,1), positives N(d,1), d = sqrt(2) Phi^-1(AUC target)) so the AUC is controlled from 0.55 to 0.95, with scores independent of group (no within-group dependence; an optimistic simplification). One dataset per AUC value (seed fixed), so the sample AUC differs from the target by sampling noise (listed below, and used as the x-position in the figure). The analytic curve is the infinite-sample binormal price, kept = pi r + (1-pi)(1 - Phi(d + Phi^-1(1-r))). **These are simulated, not measured**, and real score distributions need not be binormal.")
w("")
w("### 1a. Where the real stage models sit")
w("")
w("Pooled group-aware calibration + test MOFs, seed-0 models. 'Binormal at the same AUC' is the analytic curve evaluated at the model's AUC and the stage's prevalence (interpolated from the saved curve).")
w("")
w("| stage (MOFs / groups / prevalence) | model | AUC [95% CI] | " + " | ".join(f"kept at recall {r:.2f} [95% CI] (binormal)" for r in R) + " |")
w("|---|---|---|" + "---|" * len(R))
for t in TASKS:
    s = D["synthetic"][t]
    for ph, lab in (("phase2", "Phase 2"), ("phase3", "Phase 3")):
        r_ = D["real"][f"{ph}_{t}"]
        an = lambda r: np.interp(r_["auc"][0], [p["auc"] for p in s["analytic"]], [p[f"kept_{r}"] for p in s["analytic"]])
        w(f"| {t} ({r_['n']} / {r_['n_groups']} / {r_['prevalence']:.2f}) | {lab} | {ci(r_['auc'])} | " + " | ".join(f"{ci(r_[f'kept_{r}'])} ({an(r):.3f})" for r in R) + " |")
w("")
w("### 1b. Synthetic price of recall at controlled AUC")
w("")
w("Kept fraction at target recall 0.80 / 0.90 / 0.95 with group-bootstrap 95% intervals (simulated scores on each stage's real labels and groups). Sample AUC in brackets.")
w("")
w("| AUC target | " + " | ".join(f"{t}: kept @ {'/'.join(f'{r:.2f}' for r in R)}" for t in TASKS) + " |")
w("|---|" + "---|" * 3)
for i, a in enumerate(D["auc_grid"]):
    cells = []
    for t in TASKS:
        p = D["synthetic"][t]["points"][i]
        cells.append(f"({p['auc_sample']:.3f}) " + " / ".join(f"{p[f'kept_{r}'][0]:.2f} [{p[f'kept_{r}'][1]:.2f}, {p[f'kept_{r}'][2]:.2f}]" for r in R))
    w(f"| {a:.2f} | " + " | ".join(cells) + " |")
w("")
tp = D["synthetic"]["thermal"]["analytic"]
w("**Reading.**")
w(f"- Recall is expensive when discrimination is modest. For the analytic binormal curve at the thermal prevalence ({D['synthetic']['thermal']['prevalence']:.2f}), a target recall of 0.95 still keeps " + ", ".join(f"{np.interp(a, [p['auc'] for p in tp], [p['kept_0.95'] for p in tp]):.2f} at AUC {a:.2f}" for a in (0.70, 0.80, 0.90, 0.95)) + " of all MOFs; reaching a kept fraction below 0.5 at recall 0.95 would need an AUC far above any stage model here.")
w("- The real stage models lie close to the binormal curve at their own AUC for most cells (table 1a), so the binormal curve is a reasonable guide to how much an AUC improvement would buy; the deviations are listed in the table and several are within the intervals. I did not test the binormal fit formally.")
w("- The stage AUCs (about 0.64-0.78 here) imply keeping roughly " + f"{min(D['real'][f'phase3_{t}']['kept_0.9'][0] for t in TASKS):.2f}-{max(D['real'][f'phase3_{t}']['kept_0.9'][0] for t in TASKS):.2f} of MOFs at recall 0.90 for the Phase 3 models; the solvent and water stages filter little at high recall.")
w("- Synthetic points use one simulated dataset per AUC with the real sample size; their intervals reflect sampling and group structure only, and sample AUCs can differ noticeably from the target on the small water set (see brackets).")
w("")
w("## 2. Limitations")
w("")
n3 = X3["results"][0]
gp = [pa["valid"]["frac_reps_at_or_above_target"] for t in TASKS for pa in C3[f"group_{t}"]["pac"]]
sp = {r["split"]: r for r in GS["per_split"]}
w("| limitation | what it is | size / evidence | effect on the claims |")
w("|---|---|---|---|")
w(f"| Group proxy, not MOFid | groups are connected components over refcode family and DOI (DOIs exist only for solvent-table MOFs); no MOFid in the released data | {GS['n_groups']:,} groups for {GS['n_mofs']:,} MOFs; largest group {max(r['largest_group'] for r in GS['per_split'])} | Duplicates or near-duplicates in different groups would leak across splits and make group-aware metrics and conformal coverage optimistic; not measured |")
w(f"| Only {n3['n_labelled']} MOFs with all labels, {n3['n_all_stable']} positives | the cascade can be scored out-of-sample only on MOFs present in all three tables | {n3['n_labelled']} MOFs, {n3['n_all_stable']} stable at all three stages | cascade recall intervals are wide (Clopper-Pearson about [0.71, 1.00] at 16-17 of 17); consistent with the guarantee, cannot confirm it; the 5 repetitions are not independent |")
w("| Configuration-selection leak in the cascade | Phase 3 configurations were chosen by CV on the training groups of the single split and are reused in every cascade fold | some of those training MOFs lie in cascade held-out folds | small, configuration-level optimism in the Phase 3 cascade numbers; Phase 2 cascade (released hyperparameters) has no such selection |")
w(f"| 60/20/20 split | one group-aware split (seed 0): {sp['train']['mofs']:,} / {sp['cal']['mofs']:,} / {sp['test']['mofs']:,} MOFs; models see 60% of MOFs (the released scripts use 80%) | test sets 589 / 425 / 232 MOFs (thermal / solvent / water), 139-313 stable | wide intervals; a different split gives different numbers; all models are somewhat weaker than with 80% training |")
w(f"| PAC (training-conditional) variant unverified | Beta-based threshold with delta = 0.1 | partitions reaching the target: {100 * min(gp):.1f}%-{100 * max(gp):.1f}% across cells vs nominal >= 90% | do not claim a high-probability guarantee; only the marginal guarantee (mean recall >= 1 - alpha) matches the data |")
w("| Marginal, group-level exchangeability | the split conformal guarantee holds on average over random assignments of groups to calibration/test | about half of single calibration draws fall below target | a single deployed threshold can miss its target |")
w("| Released labels, no external test set | all numbers use the released tables | | recall is relative to the released labels |")
w("")
w("## 3. Figures (PDF, `figures/`)")
w("")
w("| file | content | data source |")
w("|---|---|---|")
w("| `fig1_group_vs_random.pdf` | group-aware vs random-split AUC, accuracy and thermal MAE (Phase 2 baseline models, seed 0, 95% intervals) | `phase2/metrics.json` |")
w("| `fig2_recall_vs_target.pdf` | realised test recall vs target recall per stage, Phase 2 vs Phase 3 models, 95% CI over test groups | `phase2/conformal.json`, `phase3/conformal.json` |")
w("| `fig3_kept_vs_recall.pdf` | kept fraction vs target recall per stage, both model sets, 95% CI | same |")
w("| `fig4_cascade.pdf` | cascade recall on the 17 all-stable MOFs with Clopper-Pearson intervals (dots = 5 repetitions), and kept fraction of the 92 | `phase2/cascade.json`, `phase3/cascade.json` |")
w("| `fig5_price_of_recall.pdf` | kept fraction vs AUC at recall 0.80/0.90/0.95: analytic curve, synthetic points with group-bootstrap bars, real models | `phase4/price_of_recall.json` |")
w("")
w("Colours are the Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe set and every series also differs in marker or line style; legends sit below the panels where they would overlap data. I checked the layout by rendering previews of each figure; the figures are drafts and captions, panel letters and journal sizing are not done. Fig. 1 plots the Phase 2 models only. Fig. 4's interval is Clopper-Pearson for the rounded mean count of passes out of 17, not an interval that accounts for the repetitions.")
w("")
w("Regenerate everything: `bash figures/make_all.sh` (env var `PY` selects the interpreter).")
open("notes/phase4.md", "w").write("\n".join(L) + "\n")
print("written notes/phase4.md,", len(L), "lines")
